Independent follow-up review of the Apply extraction and verified review repairs. No tools are available. Review only source provided, identify concrete actionable defects with counterexamples. Do not approve the entire release. Previous concerns fixed here: explicit yes only (empty answer is also automatic UI dismissal), post-approval dirty-state and authority rechecks, failed Git probes fail closed, completed-write result survives notification failure, abort settles its own prompt, stable catalog selection and job-manager cancellation, capability only scoped for Forge Apply, full literal preview with control-byte escapes. The service builder only grants patchApplication to agon.forge; that source excerpt follows. No claim of sandboxing or immunity to unrelated external Git writers is made. Inherited undo/token/parser backend repairs remain explicit next work, not release waivers. Assess whether any remaining concern is an actual unsafe path, not merely a missing abstraction.

